{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f0d017c4ed7e340f","name":"Tribal Shaman","source":{"id":"source:reference-f0d017c4ed7e340f","title":"Tribal Shaman","revision":25541,"timestamp":"2024-11-27T01:34:55Z","sha256":"3c74e6cb3a5e91f7d5944b04650d1ba77238def9c757d5ae6c2f2023e1a99164","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25541","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Tribal%20Shaman&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f0d017c4ed7e340f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Among primitive cultures, certain ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Adepts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Adepts"}," serve as tribal healers or witch doctors, using the power of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," to cure ailments and mend bones. In addition to their control of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", Tribal Shamans are also proficient in more mundane cures, although their techniques and methods might seem unorthodox compared to physicians in more civilized cultures. Among many groups, Tribal Shamans also serve as \"Healers of Words,\" acting as respected (and neutral) mediators between disagreeing parties. The wise words of the Tribal Shaman go a long way in repairing any damage caused by political disputes and inspire unity and confidence among their people. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although Tribal Shamans are focused on curing the sick and tending to the wounded, not all of them have taken a vow of nonviolence. Some even accompany their warriors into battle; however, their status and relative lack of fighting prowess means that they are kept to the rear of combat and protected b a cadre of their kinfolk.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Tribal Shaman Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Tribal Shamans commonly travel with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Thugs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thugs"}," (generic warriors) or even ",{"tag":"a","children":["Martial Artists"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Martial_Artists"}," (representing elite warriors of the tribe), who protect them from harm.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Because of their unique connection to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", some Tribal Shamans might be considered insane or at least more than a little strange, speaking in odd cadences and staring off into space. That said, a Tribal Shaman could also be called upon to serve as an ambassador or representative for a people, who respect their wisdom on such matters- the other party must content with the Tribal Shaman's unusual behavior, all the while trying not to disrespect the clan and it's traditions and customs.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When forced to defend themselves or their people, a Tribal Shaman might use ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Mind Trick"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mind_Trick","referenceId":"reference:5c0f83fb6ec25f33"}]}," to divert an opponent's attention or otherwise convince that individual to leave and never come back.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Tribal Shaman Statistics (CL 9)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 5/",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"}," 2/",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Adept"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Adept","referenceId":"refere